A||||12||Fierodave2001||Here's a good question ? (about Carlisle)||||5||
Z||000000||Fierodave2001||05-13-2001||11:39 AM||||Does anyone know the "GPS" location for<BR>Carlisle PA fairground ?  I'll have my GPS<BR>with me, and would like to have the address<BR>that I'm aiming for.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Archie||05-13-2001||12:13 PM||||Tell us about the GPS system, I've been thinking about getting one but I don't know enough about them yet.<P>Can't you just enter the address for Carlisle?<P>Thanks<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierodave2001||05-13-2001||01:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>Tell us about the GPS system, I've been thinking about getting one but I don't know enough about them yet.<BR>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mine is a Garmin 12,  it's a handheld unit.<BR>Works great. You can log into <A HREF="http://www.garmin.com" TARGET=_blank>www.garmin.com</A>  <BR>and download / upload maps & stuff.<P>There are more expenive units, that do more,<BR>but for what I use is for, It's great.  Mine <BR>was $150, but was on sale for 99 !!<P>Got it at a Boat store.  <P>I don't have my unit with me here at work,<BR>but, from what I remember, you need to enter the longitude and latitude you are aiming for.<P>On a trip, you can select "waypoints", and<BR>use those on the return trip.  Useful on the<BR>water.<P>Some of the big units have the city's <BR>pre-load in a database in the unit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||05-13-2001||02:41 PM||||as a land surveyor GPS is the best way to locate your self. the Govornment turned off the random errors last year and now a $100 device will put you with in 10 ft of any spot on earth. survey use a much more expenceve type that is good for 0.1 ft but you don't need it that good in a car or boat.<BR>unit that use a map are more than a lat+long<BR>type at $350 and up but are eazy to use in motion.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroHarry||05-13-2001||02:46 PM||||My personel recommendation is that even if your using GPS, please take the sunshade out of the windsheild.<BR>You'll arrive with so many less dents. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>GPS is cool though been using for 20 years in the Navy.<BR>Have a good trip see you there!<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I>||||reg||12
Z||000005||Fierodave2001||05-13-2001||04:20 PM||||I'm going to use it more for entertainment Value.<BR>It's many uses;<BR>1. Shows EST time to arrival<BR>2. Real time MPH<BR>3. AVG MPH<BR>4. Mile's traveled<BR>5. Min / Max MPH<BR>6. ALT / compass<BR>7. Sunrise / sunset times<BR>8. Shows which satilites are being used.  The<BR>   more contacted, the more exact the numbers.<BR>Here in Florida, this unit show between 5 - 20 foot signal.  At times,it has shown 1 ft !<BR>.<BR>For the long drives, I've used to keep track on the avg mph.  It is more accurate the the cars speedometer !<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/del_garman.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroHarry||05-13-2001||08:23 PM||||FieroDave,<BR>Which route are you taking and when?<BR>Just wondering if we could meet some where and drive in together the last 100 or so miles.<BR>I live in VA Beach VA but have to stay (Just for a couple more weeks) at the Hospital in Bethesda.<BR>No Im not dying or diseased, just awaiting orders back home.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Fierodave2001||05-13-2001||11:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHarry:<BR><B>FieroDave,<BR>Which route are you taking and when?<BR>Just wondering if we could meet some where and drive in together the last 100 or so miles.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Been looking at the route today, looks like<BR>the trip is going to be 1130 miles / and some 18 hours.  Leaving here on the 17th, and<BR>plan to check in the motel 6 on the 18.<BR>Planning for two day trip, and take some rest<BR>stops if needed.<P>It would be hard to schedule a meeting as I <BR>have no idea when I'll be in your area.  With<BR>towing, I won't be able to drive to fast.<P>Who knows, I might be able to do it in one day, but don't want to rush it.  Rather be<BR>safe.||||reg||6
Z||000008||FieroHarry||05-14-2001||03:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierodave2001:<BR><B> <BR>With<BR>towing, I won't be able to drive to fast.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now Dave if you keep towing that thing you'll never catch up with me in mileage! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I>||||reg||12
Z||000009||Fierodave2001||05-14-2001||07:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHarry:<BR><B> Now Dave if you keep towing that thing you'll never catch up with me in mileage!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, I've thought long and hard about the miles.  With the Daytona show I drove it there, and trailered it back.  I had many people at the show approch me saying, Man,<BR>if I had a car with low milage I'd trailer<BR>it everywhere.<P>Oh course, there are those that were talking about another car that was there, saying, aww, it's a trailer Queen.<P>Many people have different opinions on this, mine is, If I keep the miles off now, I won't<BR>in the future say, darn, I wish I'd done that.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||05-14-2001||09:15 AM||||go to <A HREF="http://www.mapblast.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mapblast.com</A>  and locate Carlisle, PA. Scan around the map for the fairgrounds, then center the cursor onthe fairgrounds and the Mapblast will tell you the GPS coordinates for the location.<P>  Make sure your GPS is set up for the normal WDSC or something like that map format, and remember the coordinates from mapblast are in Degrees minutes and decimal minutes, not degrees minuts seconds.<P> I use it alot for long trips when I have never been to the destination. Its fun, it lets you check your speedo, and once when I took my daughter to WPI in MA it actaully helped up find the place. We could not find the street we were looking for, but the arrow on the gps let us know that WPI was now 90° to the right, 0.34 miles away, now its 120° to the right... so we circled around to the right on side streets and it led us right to the front door.<P>here is another great map site: <A HREF="http://navigator2.maptech.com/homepage/index.cfm?" TARGET=_blank>http://navigator2.maptech.com/homepage/index.cfm?</A> <BR>they also give gps coordinates<BR>they have street maps, topographical maps, and nautical maps!!! for the whole US. I think they are viloating copywrite laws by posting them on a web site, but they are there now, and if you have a printer...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierodave2001||05-14-2001||09:44 AM||||Okay, thanks,  I'll try those sites.<P>I plan to put in the state locations along 95 just to entertain myself for the drive.<P>Just today, I went to the garman site and downloaded new software into my GPS !!<P>When I bought it, it had version 2.1 (1998)<BR>Now it has version 4.58 (year 2000 software)<P>It corrected some "tweeks", and according to Garmin, uses less power now due to a power saving mode.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.garmin.com" TARGET=_blank>www.garmin.com</A>     was their site. <P>Tried it,<BR>Looks like 40. 13.000 N   077. 10.058 W<BR>That's 958 miles as the crow flys<P>   Thanks again.<BR>Dave<p>[This message has been edited by Fierodave2001 (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroHarry||05-14-2001||10:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierodave2001:<BR><B> <P>Many people have different opinions on this, mine is, If I keep the miles off now, I won't<BR>in the future say, darn, I wish I'd done that.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I was just teasing you is all, Hey if mine had less than 60K i would tow also.<BR>But seeing as my baby is so high already I may as well "keep on trucking".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I>||||reg||7
